---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import PageHeader from "@oblivios/site-shared/components/PageHeader.astro";
import Print from "@oblivios/site-shared/components/Print.astro";
import { areas } from "../lib/areas.mjs";
import { decisions, sbom, fmt, longDate } from "../lib/records.mjs";
import { sources } from "../lib/site.mjs";

const gates = [
  ["Derivative identity", "Do branding, naming and attribution clearly show that ObliviOS is a distinct product?"],
  ["Source and notices", "Does the release inventory meet every source, notice and attribution duty?"],
  ["Worldwide distribution", "Which distribution, privacy, export, cryptography and telecom rules apply?"],
  ["Proprietary inputs", "May every Pixel, vendor and third-party binary be distributed?"],
  ["Public operations", "Are support, disclosure, update and recovery processes live and accurately described?"],
];
const pct = (n, of) => (100 * n) / Math.max(of, 1);
sources("status", [
  "docs/devices/support-policy.md (device support policy)",
  "The owner's statement of 2026-11-18 (the Pixel 10a is the daily phone; the Pixel 7a is the development phone)",
  "Decision 256 (the owner's intention to publish Pixel 10a images when interest shows; no date, no promise)",
  "docs/research/licensing-and-branding-review.md (licensing and branding review)",
  "sbom/README.md",
  "Decisions 171 and 244",
  "Counts are read from the decision log when the page is built; the date is the newest entry of the log.",
]);
---
<Page
  title="Status: ObliviOS"
  description="ObliviOS is source only: no images, no update service, and no supported device. Where each part stands in the decision log."
  path="/status"
  current="/status"
>
  <PageHeader crumb="Status" title="Status" lede="Where ObliviOS stands, and what is still open.">
    <Print id="c4" label="A checklist" grad="gw" viewBox="600 40 200 200" />
  </PageHeader>
  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="c lead">
      <div>
        <p class="big">ObliviOS is source only. There are no images, no update service and no supported device.</p>
        <p class="facts"><span class="num">{decisions.total}</span> decisions are on record: {decisions.accepted} accepted, {decisions.proposed} proposed, {decisions.other} superseded, dropped or closed. The bill of materials lists <span class="num">{fmt(sbom.components)}</span> components and the SHA-256 of <span class="num">{fmt(sbom.files)}</span> files. All of this is as of {longDate(decisions.latest)}.</p>
        <p class="fn"><b>Decision 171</b> defines this stage: source, records and a bill of materials, with no image, no update and no supported device.</p>
      </div>
      <Print id="c1" label="Three stacked layers" grad="gw" viewBox="0 40 200 200" />
    </div>
    <div class="c gap-top">
      <dl class="kv">
        <dt>What exists</dt><dd>Four repositories with the manifest, the platform patches, the services and the records.</dd>
        <dt>Supported devices</dt><dd>None. A device counts as supported only after it passes the entry gate of the device support policy.</dd>
        <dt>Phones that run it</dt><dd>The Pixel 10a (<code>stallion</code>), my daily phone, and the Pixel 7a (<code>lynx</code>), my development phone. This says which phones I use, not that they are supported: see <a href="/devices">Devices</a>.</dd>
        <dt>Images</dt><dd>None yet. If real interest in ObliviOS shows, I want to publish images for the Pixel 10a. I have set no date and I promise nothing: the gates below come first.</dd>
        <dt>Upstream baseline</dt><dd>GrapheneOS manifest <code>{sbom.baseline}</code></dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="band">
    <div class="c">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>The nine parts and where they stand</h2>
        <p>The decision log gives every decision a status. <b>Accepted</b> means the decision is made. <b>Proposed</b> means it is written, often built, and not accepted yet. The bars count the decisions behind each part.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="key"><span><i class="ka"></i>Accepted</span><span><i class="kp"></i>Proposed</span><span>The rest are superseded, dropped or closed.</span></p>
      <div class="bars">
        {areas.map((a) => (
          <div class="bar">
            <b>{a.title}</b>
            <svg class="t" viewBox="0 0 100 12" preserveAspectRatio="none" role="img" aria-label={`${a.acc} accepted, ${a.prop} proposed of ${a.n} decisions`}>
              <rect class="trk" width="100" height="12" />
              <rect class="ba" width={pct(a.acc, a.n).toFixed(1)} height="12" />
              <rect class="bp" x={pct(a.acc, a.n).toFixed(1)} width={pct(a.prop, a.n).toFixed(1)} height="12" />
            </svg>
            <small>{a.acc} accepted · {a.prop} proposed · {a.n} decisions</small>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="c">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>The road to a public beta</h2>
        <p>A public beta with binaries has to pass five gates. None is met, and none has to be at this stage, because it offers no binaries. Images for the Pixel 10a would be that beta, so they wait for these gates.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="steps">
        {gates.map(([t, q]) => (
          <div class="st">
            <Print id="r" label="An open ring: not met" />
            <h3>{t}</h3>
            <p>{q}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="prose gap-top-lg">
        <h2>What has not been reviewed</h2>
        <p>The legal review of this stage was done by an AI agent, not by qualified counsel. I build ObliviOS alone and without a budget, so counsel was not available. I accepted each risk myself, item by item, in the licensing and branding review. Nothing there is a legal opinion.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
